Let's go back to realistic for a moment!  The environment is a _dungeon_,
for heaven's sake!  The lighting is rotten, the floors are slimy to soaked,
the "pools" may have half a foot of gunk floating on top of them that make
them every bit as stomach turning as the rest of the floor, and nearly
impossible to detect.

The answer is simple:  don't play the game in race mode.  At least 99% of
the games I get crushed in are my fault for being in too much of a hurry.

Given the environment described above, you wouldn't race through it, you'd
pause and consider every step, poking anything the least bit out of the
ordinary with a very long stick.

Since the game is non-real time, don't take a step without first taking a
look.  In every circumstance where your survival is at stake, take the time
(in a great game, half an hour may be just right) to consider every possible
way to save your bacon before taking the next action.  If you can't or won't
do this (I've saved games and gone away for a day to think about it) don't
come whining about how "unfair" the game is; notice instead the long list of
folks who say they've won it.  Is it possible that they are doing something
right that you are neglecting?

Had it up to _here_ with this bellyaching stuff!

